片刻之后，第二列朝相反方向行驶的列车撞上了残骸。一个男人突然从轨道旁出现，靠近吉普车停放的地方。然后他走向了破坏现场。胡安·阿尔瓦雷斯跑向残骸，接近了一名仅受轻伤并从Metrolink 100次列车逃出的乘客。胡安问他发生了什么事。他被告知火车撞车了，有人死了。胡安惊呼：“哦，不”，然后倒在地上。有人问他是否与这次碰撞有关。胡安没有回答。相反，他站起来继续向前走。

24
00:22:10.000 --> 00:23:15.000
As he walked amongst the injured and dying, Juan held onto a large eagle feather that he carried with him everywhere. He believed that the eagle was an honored animal that guided the souls of the dead to God. By having the feather with him at that moment, Juan felt he was assisting the dying passengers to enter heaven. Raymunda Basana was going about her typical morning in Glendale when, at 6.15am, Juan Alvarez entered her home. Raymunda was Juan's landlady and the pair had a good relationship. In lieu of paying monetary rent, Juan worked as a maintenance man for Raymunda. That day, Raymunda was disturbed to find Juan in her home with his arms and chest covered in blood. Clutched tightly in his hand was a pair of blooded scissors.
当他在伤者和垂死者中行走时，胡安紧紧抓着他随身携带的一根大鹰羽毛。他相信鹰是一种受人尊敬的动物，能引导死者的灵魂去见上帝。在那一刻随身带着羽毛，胡安觉得自己在帮助垂死的乘客进入天堂。雷蒙达·巴萨纳（Raymunda Basana）正在格伦代尔过着她典型的早晨，这时，凌晨6点15分，胡安·阿尔瓦雷斯进入了她的家。雷蒙达是胡安的房东，两人关系很好。胡安不付现金房租，而是为雷蒙达做维修工。那天，雷蒙达不安地发现胡安在她的家里，手臂和胸口沾满了血。他手里紧紧抓着一把带血的剪刀。

25
00:23:15.000 --> 00:24:27.000
Juan took Raymunda's phone. He phoned his wife, speaking in a garbled mixture of Spanish and English. He then called a cousin who had supported him throughout his time in LA. He left him a voicemail. I didn't mean this. A lot of innocent people died. I don't deserve to live. I apologize for everything. Please pray for me. Please. As he made the calls, Juan stabbed himself in the chest with the scissors. Raymunda contacted 911. Juan told first responders that he had, quote, Hurt those people. I jumped in front of the train. Officers arrived at the hospital while Juan Alvarez was undergoing treatment for his self-inflicted, non-life-threatening stab wounds. Juan asked how the people on the trains were before explaining what he had done. He added,
胡安拿走了雷蒙达的电话。他给妻子打了电话，用西班牙语和英语的混合语含糊不清地说话。然后他给一位在他洛杉矶期间一直支持他的表弟打了电话。他留下了语音留言。“我不是故意的。很多无辜的人死了。我不配活着。我为一切道歉。请为我祈祷。求你了。”在打电话时，胡安用剪刀刺向自己的胸口。雷蒙达联系了911。胡安告诉急救人员，他“伤害了那些人。我跳到了火车前面。”警察到达医院时，胡安·阿尔瓦雷斯正在接受自残、无生命危险的刺伤治疗。胡安询问火车上的人情况如何，然后解释了他所做的事情。他补充说，

26
00:24:27.000 --> 00:25:33.000
I want life or death row. I deserve it. Juan was arrested and held in custody. Described as distraught and remorseful but cooperative, he was charged with one count of arson, one count of train wrecking with intent to cause derailment, and 11 counts of first-degree murder with special circumstances. Special circumstances arose due to there being multiple victims, and so, if found guilty, Juan faced the death penalty. Carmelita visited her husband while he was in custody. She told the Washington Post about the moment he decided not to end his own life, quote, He was there and out of nowhere he saw a light, not the light from the train. He said he felt like there was a presence from God telling him to get away.
“我想要终身监禁或死刑。我罪有应得。”胡安被捕并被拘留。他被描述为心烦意乱、充满悔恨但很配合，被控一项纵火罪、一项蓄意导致脱轨的火车破坏罪，以及11项带有特殊情况的一级谋杀罪。特殊情况是因为有多个受害者，因此，如果罪名成立，胡安将面临死刑。卡梅利塔在胡安被拘留期间探望了他。她告诉《华盛顿邮报》他决定不结束自己生命的那一刻，“他在那里，突然间他看到了一道光，不是火车的光。他说他感觉上帝的存在告诉他离开。”

27
00:25:33.000 --> 00:26:33.000
The restraining order that Carmelita had previously placed on Juan was also in part to his mental state. His behavior had increasingly become erratic and threatening lately. He exhibited paranoia and obsessive jealousy and accused her of cheating on him with his cousin, neighbors, co-workers, and strangers. He suspected Carmelita recorded him with hidden cameras in his bedroom. He also believed she was making pornography videos with other people. Juan purchased a firearm and repeatedly threatened Carmelita's lovers, all of whom were figments of his imagination. He even considered killing Carmelita. Juan was opposed to seeking psychiatric help, so Carmelita sought a restraining order to protect herself and their children.
卡梅利塔之前对胡安申请的限制令也部分是因为他的精神状态。他的行为最近变得越来越古怪和具有威胁性。他表现出偏执和强迫性的嫉妒，指责她与他的表弟、邻居、同事和陌生人有染。他怀疑卡梅利塔在他的卧室里安装了隐藏摄像头监视他。他还认为她和别人在拍色情录像。胡安购买了枪支，并多次威胁卡梅利塔的情人，所有这些人都是他想象出来的。他甚至考虑过杀死卡梅利塔。胡安反对寻求精神病治疗，所以卡梅利塔寻求限制令来保护自己和他们的孩子。

28
00:26:33.000 --> 00:27:39.000
This caused Juan's lifelong suicidal inclination to re-emerge. He had told others of his intentions to end his life. In preparation for the trial, Juan Ávarez was interviewed by a number of psychiatrists. Juan diagnosed him with a psychotic mood disorder and attributed Juan's impulsive behavior and irritability to this disorder. Another psychiatrist was of the opinion that Juan showed logical, goal-oriented behavior on the day of the train crash. Others theorized that Juan's desire to end his own life was the result of a depressing come-down of a methamphetamine high, which he admitted to using prior to the train crash. On the morning of the train crash, Juan recalled Carmelita belittling him from the backseat of his Jeep as he drove around searching for the ideal place to take his life.
这导致胡安终身的自杀倾向再次出现。他曾向他人表达过结束自己生命的意图。在审判准备阶段，胡安·阿尔瓦雷斯接受了几位精神病学家的采访。胡安诊断他患有精神病性心境障碍，并将胡安冲动的行为和易怒归因于这种障碍。另一位精神病学家认为，胡安在火车事故当天表现出逻辑性、目标导向的行为。其他人则推测，胡安结束自己生命的愿望是甲基苯丙胺兴奋后的抑郁后果，他承认在火车事故前使用过。在火车事故那天早上，胡安回忆起卡梅利塔在他开车四处寻找结束生命的最佳地点时，在后座贬低他。

29
00:27:39.000 --> 00:28:36.000
At one point, she was joined by a man Juan identified as one of her lovers. However, there were no others in the vehicle at the time. They were delusions. During this bickering, Juan contemplated visiting Carmelita at work and killing her, but it was too early for her to be there. Even though Juan knew that Carmelita couldn't be in two places at once, he was still convinced she was sitting behind him with another man. He heard the pair remarking, Look at how stupid he is. He can't even see us. Their words angered Juan and his attention turned to the railway tracks. He believed if he took his life there, it would get Carmelita's attention and make her feel bad.
有一次，一个男人加入了她，胡安认定那是她的情人之一。然而，当时车里没有其他人。那是幻觉。在这次争吵中，胡安考虑去卡梅利塔工作的地方杀了她，但她还没到那里。尽管胡安知道卡梅利塔不可能同时出现在两个地方，但他仍然确信她正坐在他身后，和另一个男人在一起。他听到两人评论说：“看他有多蠢。他甚至看不到我们。”他们的话激怒了胡安，他的注意力转向了铁轨。他认为如果他在那里结束生命，会引起卡梅利塔的注意，让她感到难过。

30
00:28:36.000 --> 00:29:41.000
Juan maintained that he didn't realize a passenger train would approach. He expected a cargo train that would smash through his car and continue along without derailing. He claimed he wasn't thinking about the consequences of his actions, including that others could be harmed or killed by his plan. He knew of an instance wherein a train collided with a taxi. The taxi's occupants were killed, but no one on the train was harmed. Juan Alvarez's trial began in late April 2008. His defense team insisted that Juan never intended for anyone to be hurt by his actions. He wanted to take his own life, but changed his mind at the last moment. This desire had lingered since childhood, prompted by physical and sexual abuse, drug dependency, untreated mental health issues, and a failing marriage.
胡安坚持认为他没有意识到客运列车会驶来。他以为是一列货运列车，会撞穿他的车，然后继续行驶而不会脱轨。他声称他没有考虑自己行为的后果，包括其他人可能会因为他的计划而受到伤害或死亡。他知道一个火车与出租车相撞的例子。出租车里的乘客死了，但火车上没有人受伤。胡安·阿尔瓦雷斯的审判于2008年4月下旬开始。他的辩护团队坚持认为胡安从未打算让任何人受到伤害。他想结束自己的生命，但在最后一刻改变了主意。这种愿望自童年以来一直挥之不去，是由身体和性虐待、药物依赖、未治疗的心理健康问题和失败的婚姻引起的。

